# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TP Writer FE — environment template. Copy to .env.local (gitignored)
# and fill in. Vite inlines these at build time, so set them BEFORE
# `pnpm dev` / `pnpm build`. All vars MUST be prefixed VITE_ to reach
# the browser bundle.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Backend API base URL.
#
#   Local dev (same-origin via vite proxy):
#     Leave empty or omit — client.ts falls back to `/api` and
#     vite.config.ts proxies `/api/*` → `http://localhost:3001/*`.
#     Session cookies work same-origin, no CORS dance.
#
#   Deployed FE talking to a separate BE host:
#     Set the full origin, e.g. https://api.tpwriter.com
#     The BE must then allow this FE origin in CORS_ORIGINS and set
#     session cookies with sameSite=None;Secure (prod only).
VITE_API_URL=
